    "task": "You're hiring a senior UX designer for an AI product and arrive from a LinkedIn message. What do you do first?",
    "checks": [
     "The first screen says who this is and what they do, in plain words",
     "The kind of work (AI, research, product) is clear without scrolling",
     "One primary action (see the work) stands out"
    ]
   },
   {
    "n": 2,
    "slug": "find-the-work",
    "name": "Find the work",
    "task": "You want to see their most relevant project. Where do you click?",
    "checks": [
     "A case study is one click from the first screen",
     "Projects are labelled by the problem or outcome, not only a client name or image",
     "The most relevant project for an AI role can be picked out without opening them all"
    ]
   },
   {
    "n": 3,
    "slug": "judge-the-evidence",
    "name": "Judge the evidence",
    "task": "You're on a case study. Find what this designer did personally, and what changed because of it.",
    "checks": [
     "The designer's own role is stated",
     "An outcome or evidence is stated, or why it can't be shared",
     "A summary near the top gives the problem, role and outcome"
    ]
   },
   {
    "n": 4,
    "slug": "get-in-touch",
    "name": "Get in touch",
    "task": "You'd like to invite them to interview. How do you get in touch?",
    "checks": [
     "A contact route is visible from the case study, not just the homepage",
     "Contact needs no form, or the form asks only for essentials",
     "Availability or what happens next is stated"
    ]
   },
   {
    "n": 5,
    "slug": "reassurance",
    "name": "Reassurance",
    "task": "Before reaching out, you want to check they're credible. Where do you look?",
    "checks": [
     "Independent proof (a named testimonial, publication or client) sits near the work",
     "Real identity is clear: full name, LinkedIn, location",
     "The site looks current: dates, current role"
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
